# Go-to-market docs home (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-08):

> **Move and centralize positioning, marketing, website design, pricing,
> CMMC and competitive analysis into
> `https://github.com/analoginfo-pim/pam-platform-docs/tree/main/docs`.
> Going forward use the centralized repo of competitive analysis.**

## The rule

> **New and revised positioning, marketing, website / operator-UI design
> doctrine, pricing, Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC)
> competitive notes, competitor analysis, and pricing / competitive-
> selling Cursor canvases are authored in
> `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/`. Product repos keep pointers
> only. Implementation gap inventories and closeable coding plans stay
> in the owning product repo. Do not leave unique list-price or
> competitive-selling canvases only in the local IDE `canvases/`
> folder.**

## Home

[https://github.com/analoginfo-pim/pam-platform-docs/tree/main/docs/go-to-market](https://github.com/analoginfo-pim/pam-platform-docs/tree/main/docs/go-to-market)

Index: `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/README.md`

| Work | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Competitive analysis, CMMC market map, pricing briefs, GTM, website/UI doctrine | `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/` |
| Pricing / competitive-selling Cursor canvases | `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/canvases/` (index: `canvases/README.md`; GitHub-readable CMMC rate card: `pricing/azure-cmmc-hosted-price-list.md`) |
| Anonymized buyer RFP playbook | `pam-platform-docs/docs/commercial/rfp-competitive-roadmap/` |
| Control-by-control gap / closeable plan | Owning product `docs/dev/` (for example `cmmc-800-53-full-gap-analysis.md`) |

## Forbidden

- Adding a new competitor matrix, CMMC enclave market note, price briefing,
  GTM/strategy paper, or pricing / competitive-selling canvas under
  `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/` or `docs/business/`
- Leaving unique list-price or competitive-selling canvas edits only in
  `~/.cursor/projects/*/canvases/`
- Treating a product-repo stub as the living document
- Claiming Met / certified from a competitive note

## Required agent behavior

1. Edit the file under `go-to-market/` (or add a new one there and index it
   in `README.md`). Pricing / competitive canvases go in
   `go-to-market/canvases/` plus a GitHub-readable markdown twin when the
   canvas is a rate card.
2. Keep any product-repo path as a short pointer to GitHub `pam-platform-docs`.
3. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set.
4. After a canvas change, copy the same `.canvas.tsx` into the local IDE
   `canvases/` folder if an interactive view is needed. The repo copy is
   the source of truth.

